  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to UN DPPA Multi-Year Appeal 2023-2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The DPPA Multi-Year Appeal (MYA) 2023&#x2013;2026 is the Department of Political and Peacebuilding Affairs&#x2019; main voluntary funding mechanism to support conflict prevention, mediation, and peacebuilding efforts worldwide. It outlines how DPPA seeks Member States&#x2019; financial contributions to sustain and expand its operations in preventing violent conflict and building durable peace. 

Through the MYA, the DPPA supplements its regular UN budget to fund flexible, rapid-response initiatives such as:
&#x2022; Strengthening preventive diplomacy and mediation;
&#x2022; Supporting UN political and peacekeeping missions;
&#x2022; Providing analysis and early warning capacities;
&#x2022; Enabling partnerships with regional organizations and civil society;
&#x2022; Advancing youth, women, and inclusive participation in peace processes.

Structured around four thematic funding windows&#x2014;Rapid Response, Women, Peace and Security, Technology and Innovation, and Local Peace Initiatives&#x2014;the Appeal sustains fields operations through i.e., special political missions support special envoys and strengthens analytical and early warning capacities. About 70 percent of MYA funds are unearmarked, ensuring operational agility and responsiveness to emerging crises.</narrative>
  </description>
